Heritage attribution

Undercroft began as a fork of the MemPalace project
(https://github.com/MemPalace/mempalace), a Python AI-memory system published
under the MIT License, and its feature surface was ported to Rust. The two
have since diverged completely: no Python remains, Undercroft contains no
source code from MemPalace, and the vault and security layer, the retrieval
stack, the language layer and the orchestrator have no MemPalace counterpart.
The feature-by-feature relationship is documented in docs/PARITY.md.

